{"description": "Thinner is a horror novel by American author Stephen King, published in 1984 by NAL under King's pseudonym Richard Bachman. The story centers on lawyer Billy Halleck, who kills a crossing Romani woman in a road accident and escapes legal punishment because of his connections. However, the woman's father places a curse on Halleck, which causes him to lose weight uncontrollably.", "links": [{"title": "StephenKing.com - Thinner", "url": "https://www.stephenking.com/library/bachman_novel/thinner.html", "type": {"key": "/type/link"}}, {"title": "Thinner (novel) - Wikipedia", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Thinner_(novel)", "type": {"key": "/type/link"}}, {"title": "THINNER by Richard Bachman | Kirkus Reviews", "url": "https://www.kirkusreviews.com/book-reviews/richard-bachman-3/thinner/", "type": {"key": "/type/link"}}, {"title": "Rereading Stephen King, chapter 19: Thinner", "url": "https://www.theguardian.com/books/booksblog/2013/apr/16/rereading-stephen-king-thinner", "type": {"key": "/type/link"}}, {"title": "The Great Stephen King Re-read: Thinner", "url": "https://www.tor.com/2013/01/31/the-great-stephen-king-re-read-thinner/", "type": {"key": "/type/link"}}], "title": "Thinner", "covers": [8274288, 10936333, 11737195, 12373117, -1, 14487305, 10200833, 13916882, 13916883, 13916887, 13158140], "first_sentence": {"type": "/type/text", "value": "\"Thinner,\" the old Gypsy man with the rotting nose whispers to William Halleck as Halleck and his wife, Heidi, come out of the court-house."}, "subject_places": ["\u00c9tats-Unis", "Connecticut", "New York City", "Fairview", "Maine", "Milford"], "first_publish_date": "June 1985", "subject_people": ["Bob", "Bobby", "Jillian", "Marcy", "Timmy", "Lars Arncaster", "Ron Baker", "Mrs. Bean", "Judy Blume", "Hilmer Boynton", "Mrs. Callaghee", "Allen Chalker", "Richard Crosskill", "Georgina Deever", "David Duganfield", "Lonnie Enders", "Mr. Fander", "Rand Foxworth", "Richard Ginelli", "Heidi Halleck", "Linda J